** ==============================================================================
** ABAQUS/STANDARD THERMO-MECHANICAL MATERIAL CARD: INCONEL FILLER METAL 82
** Nickel filler wire ERNiCr-3 (AWS A5.14, ISO 18274 S Ni 6082), weld deposit
** Nominal composition 72 Ni - 20 Cr - 3 Mn - 2.5 Nb - 1.5 Fe (wt%)
** Units: mm, s, tonne, mJ, MPa, C
** Author: Victor Maia (vhfm08@gmail.com)
**
** ESTIMATED DATA, FIRST APPROXIMATION. No measurement of this wire is behind this
** card. Values come from public producer data for INCONEL Filler Metal 82 and for
** the base alloy of the same family (INCONEL alloy 600, which has close Ni-Cr
** contents), read to two or three figures.
**
** Plain material, no phase transformation framework: the deposit is austenitic
** (fcc) from the solidus to room temperature, with no solid-state transformation.
** Dilution with the steel and the cast iron is not modelled in this card; the
** fusion zone composition is a post-processing step (Schaeffler diagram).
** Consequences in the deck:
**  - no *DEPVAR: *INITIAL CONDITIONS, TYPE=SOLUTION must not include FILLER
**    (use an element set of the two phase transformation materials only);
**  - the filler elements are switched on by *MODEL CHANGE, ADD.
**
** Values and their origin:
**  - Melting range 1300-1350 C (producer data for the filler metal); latent heat
**    of fusion 300 kJ/kg (nickel alloy handbook range 290-310 kJ/kg).
**  - Density 8.30 g/cm3 at 20 C, falling with the thermal expansion, 7.60 in the
**    liquid.
**  - Conductivity, specific heat, elastic modulus and mean expansion: alloy 600
**    curves. Liquid conductivity: 3 x the solid value above the liquidus, as in
**    the steel and cast iron cards (stirring of the weld pool).
**  - Strength of the as-welded deposit at 20 C: Rp0.2 = 380 MPa, Rm = 640 MPa,
**    elongation 40 % (producer typical values). Yield stress versus temperature:
**    1.00 / 0.92 / 0.87 / 0.80 / 0.60 / 0.30 / 0.10 of the 20 C value at 20 / 300
**    / 500 / 700 / 800 / 1000 / 1200 C, from the elevated temperature data of
**    alloy 600; liquid floor of 5 MPa above the solidus.
**  - Annealing at the liquidus: the plastic strain is reset when the deposit
**    melts, like in the steel and cast iron cards.
**
** References:
**  - Special Metals, INCONEL Filler Metal 82, product data sheet
**  - Special Metals, INCONEL alloy 600, publication SMC-027
**  - AWS A5.14/A5.14M, Specification for Nickel and Nickel-Alloy Bare Welding
**    Electrodes and Rods
